Ray Norton"] " was made clearly out of the zone. Norton slowed dramatically, trying to keep the exchange legal, and the Germans went ahead, although Norton had a slight lead by the second exchange, outrunning Hary. Another poor exchange occurred however, and at the final exchange, Lauer had a two-metre lead on " [:a {:href "/athletes/79042"} "Dave Sime"] ". Sime ran one of the great anchor legs to bring the US home in what was at first thought to be a world record 39.4 (39.59). But the US was properly disqualified and the Germans won the gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bronze medalists Great Britain were lucky not to be also disqualified as film footage of their first handover appeared to show " [:a {:href "/athletes/69409"} "Peter Radford"] " receiving the baton outside the exchange zone."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Unified Team of Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "39.5 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "39.7 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "39.5 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/70195"} "Bernd Cullmann"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/70267"} "Armin Hary"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/70395"} "Walter Mahlendorf"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/70375"} "Martin Lauer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/70248"} "Manfred Germar"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/70525"} "Manfred Steinbach"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Soviet Union"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding